━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
## CODING RULES — FOLLOW STRICTLY
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

1.  Django is the ONLY place for business logic, DB access, and AI calls.
2.  Streamlit ONLY renders UI and calls Django API via requests. No DB. No AI.
3.  All Django API views must use DRF APIView or ViewSet classes.
4.  JWT token stored in st.session_state["token"] — check on every protected page.
5.  Use Django ORM exclusively. No raw SQL anywhere.
6.  Use Django's PASSWORD_HASHERS with bcrypt. Never store plain text passwords.
7.  Enable CORS in Django using django-cors-headers for Streamlit origin.
8.  All OpenAI calls in gpt_extractor.py only. Wrapped in try/except.
9.  Use st.form() in Streamlit for all input forms.
10. Use python-dotenv in both services. Never hardcode secrets.
11. Run migrations before first use: python manage.py makemigrations && migrate.
12. Both services start independently:
      Backend  → python manage.py runserver 8000
      Frontend → streamlit run app.py

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
## WHAT NOT TO USE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

✗ HuggingFace — not allowed
✗ LangChain — not needed, direct OpenAI SDK only
✗ Flask / FastAPI — Django only for backend
✗ SQLAlchemy — Django ORM only
✗ Any third-party auth library — JWT via simplejwt only

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
## ACCURACY BENCHMARK TARGET
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Target : 90%+ field extraction accuracy
Method : Compare GPT-4o output vs manually filled Excel ground truth
Test   : Minimum 10 different resumes
Track  : Per-field accuracy (name, email, skills, projects, etc.)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

When I say "build X", generate production-ready code for that module
following all rules above. Always show the full file. Never truncate.
Start every file with a comment block: filename, purpose, and app it belongs to.